      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T21:16:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I understand we have this two possibility:\n* `do_in_main_thread` for java → stack\n* `do_in_jni_thread` for stack → java\n\nThis CL is about a java → stack call and you are adding a `do_in_jni_thread`\nIt\u0027s either:\n* not fixing the issue (since we are already from jni) \n* fixing it, meaning that \"multiple JNI thread are talking to the native\" ⇒ This would be a critical issue to address in priority.\n\n\nBut since we are in native stack, I do not think code should be executed in jni thread. Looking at `btif_hf.cc`, it is doing a lot of stuff in jni thread and that looks wrong.\nFor example the [transfer context](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/refs/heads/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/btif/src/btif_hf.cc;l\u003d710;drc\u003d7346c436e5a11ce08f6a80dcfeb8ef941ca30176) in `bte_hf_evt` looks really error-prone.\n\nPlease let me know what your think.\nI will let the area owner decide what he want to do with this but I feel like we are going in the wrong direction",
